WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.839 --> 00:00:01.840
Hello, I'm Andrew Garfield.

00:00:01.840 --> 00:00:03.053
And I'm Claire Foy.

00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:06.948
And I'm Andy Serkis, the 
director of the upcoming film, Breathe.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.384
We're excited to bring you this new trailer.

00:00:09.384 --> 00:00:13.700
It's based on an inspiring true story, 
and it will be in theatres this October.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:15.700
We hope you enjoy it.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.680
She's gorgeous.

00:00:21.020 --> 00:00:23.020
Sorry! My fault, sorry.

00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:26.792
You can't possibly marry him, Diana.

00:00:26.792 --> 00:00:28.246
He's practically a stranger.

00:00:28.246 --> 00:00:30.706
It's not as if you don't have other options.

00:00:30.706 --> 00:00:34.460
The thing is, I just know this is it.

00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:37.360
Oh, I've got news.

00:00:37.377 --> 00:00:37.877
Oh yeah?

00:00:37.877 --> 00:00:39.299
I'm going to have a baby.

00:00:41.399 --> 00:00:45.169
Best news I ever had since I've 
proposed and you said yeah.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:51.480
Robin!

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.180
I can't breathe.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.820
You inhaled the polio virus from droplets in the air.

00:00:57.825 --> 00:01:00.569
The result is you can't breathe for yourself.

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:02.970
You really must leave me to rot now.

00:01:04.059 --> 00:01:06.059
We can't have this.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:08.220
Apparently, I can.

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:12.900
Get me out of here.

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:20.940
No one with your husband's disability exists 
outside a hospital anywhere in the world.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:25.670
I've just had an idea.

00:01:26.479 --> 00:01:28.479
It does his breathing for him.

00:01:28.479 --> 00:01:30.450
Oh! Amazing! Hooray!

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:32.450
There'll be no stopping you now, oh boy!

00:01:40.469 --> 00:01:43.094
What exactly is it you want from me?

00:01:43.094 --> 00:01:45.647
Well, we want more of these chairs.

00:01:45.647 --> 00:01:47.178
For people like Robin.

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.043
No one's ever believed it's possible to live as you do.

00:01:53.043 --> 00:01:54.414
This is bloody marvellous.

00:01:54.414 --> 00:01:55.679
Well we should show them.

00:01:58.240 --> 00:02:00.600
When I first became paralysed, I wanted to die.

00:02:01.870 --> 00:02:03.919
But my wife wouldn't let me.

00:02:03.919 --> 00:02:08.969
She told me I had to live to see our 
son grow up, so I went on living.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:13.084
Your life is my life.

00:02:18.630 --> 00:02:21.554
Why do you keep your disabled imprisoned?

00:02:21.554 --> 00:02:24.620
Go back to your patients and set them free.

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:31.229
I've accepted the risk of dying.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.200
I don't want to just survive.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.260
I want to truly live.

